  "keywords": [
    "arduino mega",
    "mega 2560",
    "atmega2560",
    "mega2560",
    "ramps",
    "3d printer",
    "marlin"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Four hardware serial ports is the reason to pick a Mega. Serial0 on D0 and D1 is shared with USB; Serial1, Serial2 and Serial3 on D18/D19, D16/D17 and D14/D15 are free.",
    "SPI is NOT on these headers. MISO, MOSI, SCK and SS are D50 to D53 on the double-row header, and also on the 6-pin ICSP header in the Uno-standard position.",
    "I2C is D20 and D21, not A4 and A5. Uno code that assumes the analog pins will not find the bus. D20 and D21 appear twice on the header; both positions are the same net.",
    "PWM is available on D2 to D13 and on D44, D45 and D46, which are on the double-row header. Fifteen in total.",
    "The analog pins double as digital D54 to D69, so A0 is also pin 54 in code.",
    "20 mA per I/O pin maximum and 50 mA total from the 3V3 pin, which comes from a small on-board 3.3 V regulator.",
    "VIN takes 6 to 20 V, with 7 to 12 V recommended. Above that the linear regulator cooks under any real load.",
    "This is the board inside most RAMPS-based 3D printers, which is why it stays in production long after an ESP32 would do the job for less."
  ],
